  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Introduction of Chrysanthemum breeding to Vietnam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Note: The project has been withdrawn by the project partners before the implementation phase has been started.Vietnam is an important flower producing country in South-East Asian. The chrysanthemum is a popular flower due to cultural and religious ceremonies.The project will introduce flower breeding in Vietnam. It will select and develop new varieties that perform best under the local conditions and are resistant to local pests and diseases. The new varieties will be &quot;designed&quot; for the regional market.The partners are active in chrysanthemum breeding (applicant) and growing (local partner). The project fits in both companies&apos; strategies. The partners will establish a joint venture that will be located in Dalat where flower growing is wide spread. The project will boost the Vietnam chrysanthemum sector. It gets access to new high quality varieties that the local partner, outgrowers in Vietnam will grow for the Japanese, Vietnamese and other markets in the region.Flower breeding is a risky business and a certain scale is needed to increase the change to success. For the breeding a special greenhouse will be needed including a small tissue lab.The joint venture will hire around one hundred employees, most of them women. Salaries will be in line with living wage or above. The project will operate under GlobalGAP certificate what means good working conditions. The environmental impact will be strictly monitored by the Vietnamese government.</narrative>
  </description>
